{# « Demander à l'assistant », offered ONLY under the results of the local
   search (ARCHITECTURE.md §8.87) — never above them, never instead of
   them. The order is the locked decision D2: the search answers offline,
   at every role, with no provider configured; the assistant is what you
   reach for when it did not. Turning that around would make an AI call
   the first thing a visitor does to find the page they already know the
   name of.

   Rendered at all only when `help_assistant_available` is true — the
   connector is operational AND the viewer is `chief` or above (D4, D7).
   Below that, this partial produces nothing and the search is simply the
   whole feature.

   public/assets/js/help-search.js shows and hides it with the results,
   and sends the typed question STRAIGHT AWAY — the click is the question.
   There is no second field to retype it into and no second button to
   confirm it with: two search boxes one under the other on the same
   screen is the thing a reader cannot make sense of.

   Parameter:
   - inline   true when the assistant lives on this very surface (the
              help panel, which reveals it in place); false when the
              question has to travel to /aide/assistant.

   data-* only, no inline handlers (CSP — design.md §7.5). #}
{% if help_assistant_available|default(false) %}
    <div class="mt-3 pt-3 border-top" data-help-assistant-invite-zone hidden>
        {# Said once. After the first exchange the button is simply how the
           next question is asked, and help-search.js hides this line. #}
        <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2" data-help-assistant-invite-preamble>
            Aucun de ces sujets ne répond à votre question ?
        </p>
        {# Offline the answer cannot come: it is written by a provider on
           the internet. Said here rather than by hiding the button, which
           would only leave a reader wondering where it went. #}
        <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2 d-none" data-help-assistant-invite-offline>
            <i class="bi bi-wifi-off" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            Vous êtes hors connexion : l'assistant a besoin d'internet.
            Les résultats ci-dessus, eux, s'affichent sans.
        </p>

        {% if inline|default(false) %}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" data-help-assistant-invite>
                <i class="bi bi-stars" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Demander à l'assistant
            </button>
        {% else %}
            <a href="/aide/assistant" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" data-help-assistant-invite>
                <i class="bi bi-stars" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Demander à l'assistant
            </a>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
